+// SA-nx: main RAM (area 3 and its mirrors in P0 to P3) is most of every frame's accesses, and the
+// general resolve() walks P4, operand-cache RAM and the area switch before getting there; the
+// profile on Mark's PC put resolve() alone at 10% of the game thread. The same address test as
+// resolve()'s area 3 case: physical = a & 0x1FFFFFFF, area = physical >> 26.
+constexpr bool is_main_ram(std::uint32_t a) noexcept {
+    return a < 0xE0000000u && ((a >> 26) & 7u) == 3u;
+}
